  "title": "Ha\u1e6dallu",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/people"
  ],
  "details": "<p>According to an Akkadian inscription of Ninurta-kudurr\u012b-u\u1e63ur of Suhu, the Ha\u1e6dallu, together with other Aramean tribal groups, attacked the land L\u0101q\u00ea. The Ha\u1e6dallu and their allies were defeated by Ninurta-kudurr\u012b-u\u1e63ur. The Assyrian king Tiglath-pileser III also fought with them during his first regnal year.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The name of a nomadic Aramean tribal group that was active in the middle Euphrates region during the early part of the first millennium B.C. and in Babylonia in the middle of the eighth century B.C.",
  "reprPoint": null,
